    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1193">

                <pb facs="1070" n="756" xml:id="pg756"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72114/432</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-30">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">December 30, 1914</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Your 1148, 19th. Circular instruction, November 20, regarding reports on
                    detention camps, issued because Department did not desire its diplomatic
                    officers should be subject to charge of partiality, a probable result if
                    diplomatic officers undertook generally, the responsibility of advising the
                    countries at war regarding conditions of camps where their officers and men were
                    detained.</p>
                <p>In view of German Government’s request, the Department will inquire of the
                    British Government whether there is objection to your appointment of some one to
                    investigate German detention camps in England.</p>
                <p>Your December 23, 1 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1193-f1"/> With approval German
                    authorities representative of Embassy may visit detention camp at Burg.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
